<i>TURN</i>

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:14.590
<i>TURN-A</i>

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:15.590
<i>TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:16.090
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:16.510
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:17.510
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:18.180
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:20.680
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:27.940
<i>Even though I am of the Moonrace, I was overwhelmed by the massive facility known as the Zacktraeger.</i>

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:36.150
<i>The Dianna Counter Army was also stationed there, and they nearly entered into a battle against the Willgem.</i>

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:42.330
<i>Fortunately, Queen Dianna and Lady Kihel's quick thinking...</i>

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:45.040
<i>...allowed the Willgem to safely depart the facility.</i>

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:56.170
<b>The Militia's Decisive Space Battle</b>

00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:07.730
Does that camera work out here?

00:02:07.730 --> 00:02:09.520
That's what I'm testing.

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:13.230
If I need to, I'll use the camera which the soldiers at Zacktraeger gave me.

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:15.030
Is that so?

00:02:15.030 --> 00:02:18.740
Are there any newspapers on the moon who'd be interested in buying your photos?

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:20.040
If there aren't any newspapers...

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:24.080
...there are other collectors, or the people on the Daily net who'll pay a decent amount.

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:26.410
After all, it's proof that we were able to make this artifact fly.

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:29.330
Miss Fran Doll...

00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:34.250
Do you believe the rumors that suggest my sister was on the Soleil, posing as Dianna?

00:02:34.250 --> 00:02:36.920
I can't help but believe them.

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:42.430
My sister's the type who always wanted to learn through her actions and experiences, that's why she never attended college.

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:43.930
Aren't you the same way, Sochie?

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:47.930
During this war, you learned to pilot a mobile suit, and now you're learning to move in zero-g.

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:49.730
I guess so.

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:52.230
Aren't you coming too, Fran?

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:53.940
I'd like to take a few more shots.

00:02:56.650 --> 00:02:58.150
Loran...
- Yes?

00:02:58.150 --> 00:03:00.950
Hey, when will we toss out the things in the chest?

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:03.740
This isn't the proper time yet.

00:03:05.330 --> 00:03:08.330
I'd rather wait and do it when we're even further from the Earth.

00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:10.120
You mean because of their poison?

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:11.250
Exactly.

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:12.920
Is this where you were?

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:18.050
That's dangerous!

00:03:18.710 --> 00:03:19.920
Oops...!

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:21.220
Milady Kihel!

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:22.640
Watch out, sis!

00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:26.720
Please, be more careful until you're a bit more used to moving in zero gravity.

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:28.220
Out of my way!

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:39.150
Zero Gravity makes it very difficult to move about...

00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:41.150
But it's also kind of fun.

00:03:41.150 --> 00:03:44.820
If we were still children, we'd almost certainly be playing "Wolf and Sheep"

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:46.620
Then let's do it anyway!

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:48.740
Okay, but Loran is the Wolf!

00:03:48.740 --> 00:03:50.540
Right. Loran...

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:53.920
Not me!

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:56.540
My sister and myself are the sheep. Come and get us!

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:59.130
Over here, Mr. Wolf!

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:01.720
So, I guess that makes me the Wolf?

00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:17.820
Goodness me...

00:04:22.150 --> 00:04:23.320
Get away!

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:27.450
I'm right here, what are you doing?

00:04:31.950 --> 00:04:36.420
I never thought it'd be so hard to stop moving when you're weightless...

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:41.050
Is there some sort of problem?

00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:42.920
It's just that you're upside down.

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:45.220
You're the one who's upside down!

00:04:45.220 --> 00:04:47.050
Is this what the moon is like?

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:49.430
Then why are we heading to a place like that?

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:52.520
We should go force that noble brat to turn the ship back towards earth.

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:56.350
However, now that this ship is on course for the moon, redirecting it would prove rather difficult.

00:04:56.350 --> 00:04:58.230
How are you holding up?

00:04:58.230 --> 00:05:00.440
What are you doing up there on the ceiling?

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:03.150
How about you, Ladderum? Is all the dizziness giving you nosebleeds?

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:04.950
Oh, this is just a leak.

00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:11.450
It's a traditional Moonrace remedy to help reduce space sickness. Mr. Harry showed it to me.

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:13.540
How's that?

00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:16.750
Now the only pain I feel's in the spot where my hair's being pulled...

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:19.540
This is the easiest way to cure a headache here in space.

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:20.840
Is that better?

00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:23.550
Some things work, and some things don't...

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:27.630
How long do you think it's been since we've played Sheep and Wolf?

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:29.050
Three or four years, perhaps.

00:05:29.050 --> 00:05:31.140
Marsha was still working for us at the time.

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:32.510
Has it really?

00:05:32.510 --> 00:05:35.730
It feels like it's been much longer than that.

00:05:35.730 --> 00:05:40.650
Well, everything that happened before the war feels like it was ages ago.

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:42.440
You should have your hair cut, you know.

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:43.820
No.

00:05:43.820 --> 00:05:45.650
All it'll do is get in everyone's way!

00:05:47.450 --> 00:05:49.110
What is it?

00:05:49.110 --> 00:05:55.330
If I use some of Queen Dianna's hair gel, my hair becomes perfectly manageable.

00:05:56.120 --> 00:06:00.830
I doubt she gave it to you. You probably just swiped some on your own.

00:06:00.830 --> 00:06:02.540
It's alright.

00:06:02.540 --> 00:06:06.220
I hereby decree that Sochie of the Earth is allowed to use it!

00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:08.930
Why are you acting like a Queen out here?

00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:10.220
What happened?

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:13.060
- Get moving!
- It looks like we're trapped!

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:14.350
What're you up to?

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:17.850
There's a lot of data that needs to be input.

00:06:17.850 --> 00:06:22.230
I was referring to the fact that you're sitting on the ceiling!

00:06:22.230 --> 00:06:24.440
Actually, you guys are the ones who're upside down.

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:28.820
My masters are taking a shower in there, so I'm staying here to make sure nothing happens.

00:06:28.820 --> 00:06:32.240
Alright, I get it. Hey, space yourselves out up there!

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:35.740
It's tickling my feet...

00:06:35.740 --> 00:06:39.620
There's a device here which siphons the water out from the floor drains.

00:06:42.040 --> 00:06:44.420
Can't we stop it from tickling my feet?

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:50.430
When we return to the earth, you're going to have to complete the Coming of Age Ceremony.

00:06:51.140 --> 00:06:55.060
But this time, I won't be in Nocis city.

00:06:55.060 --> 00:06:58.930
Loran mentioned that you never completed the holy markings ceremony.

00:06:58.930 --> 00:07:02.230
That's right... so perhaps we'll do it all over again?

00:07:02.230 --> 00:07:06.150
Somehow, it seems like the White Doll has continually become more efficient, doesn't it.

00:07:14.450 --> 00:07:15.740
L.. Ladies!

00:07:18.950 --> 00:07:20.040
I'm coming in!

00:07:29.210 --> 00:07:30.340
Stopped it.

00:07:30.630 --> 00:07:32.130
You two alright?

00:07:32.930 --> 00:07:34.220
Can you breathe?

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:41.230
Is this it?

00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:45.440
This hair got clogged in the drain,

00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:46.650
Lady Kihe..

00:07:47.230 --> 00:07:48.650
I'm terribly sorry!

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:51.530
Forgive my rudeness!

00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:55.530
I didn't mean to look at Lady Kihel's rear!

00:07:55.820 --> 00:07:56.950
Moron!

00:07:57.240 --> 00:08:00.750
It's no good... how can I return to earth now?

00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:06.420
Thank you, Loran. You saved us.

00:08:16.430 --> 00:08:19.350
Umm... You guys can breathe now, right?

00:08:19.930 --> 00:08:21.430
Thanks for the help.

00:08:21.430 --> 00:08:23.230
Isn't that funny?

00:08:23.230 --> 00:08:26.020
This time, Loran's the one who dived in the water and saved us. Right?

00:08:27.650 --> 00:08:29.940
Oh, it was nothing.

00:08:29.940 --> 00:08:32.030
I'll watch it more carefully next time.

00:08:32.030 --> 00:08:33.530
Loran... Thank you.

00:08:37.450 --> 00:08:39.950
Despite us being in space, it feels more like old times now.

00:08:40.740 --> 00:08:42.540
I guess that takes care of that.

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:45.920
Everything is so irritating in space...

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:49.920
The fact that I can't open a window up here makes me wanna scream!

00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:52.710
You've gotta drink like a dumb baby up here...

00:08:55.130 --> 00:08:56.930
Hey, look at that!

00:08:56.930 --> 00:09:00.220
What, are you a goldfish now?

00:09:00.220 --> 00:09:04.140
Oh Lord.... We're not a bunch of fishes!

00:09:04.140 --> 00:09:05.940
The sake barrel?

00:09:06.230 --> 00:09:09.150
Even the sake barrel's gettin' wasted!

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:13.940
Get that sake barrel down here!

00:09:15.740 --> 00:09:20.450
Ya know, back in the old days, I rode a barrel like this from Sunset Valve...

00:09:20.450 --> 00:09:23.750
...and floated down the river to reach Nocis!

00:09:23.750 --> 00:09:25.910
Yeah, I did it too, baby!

00:09:25.910 --> 00:09:29.420
But we don't got no rivers up here, Sir!

00:09:31.340 --> 00:09:40.550
I'll just ride n' this barrel and coast along that dang gravity thing til I go woosh and smash into earth.

00:09:40.550 --> 00:09:45.140
The wood on this here barrel's over a hundred years old. I betcha won't last half a day!

00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:47.140
Alright, Get that top on tight!

00:09:47.850 --> 00:09:49.940
How's he gonna get out when he gets there?

00:09:49.940 --> 00:09:52.520
It'll just break down when he passes through the atmosphere.

00:09:52.940 --> 00:09:54.740
I'll be the next one who goes...!

00:09:54.740 --> 00:09:56.320
No, Imma goin' next!

00:09:57.240 --> 00:09:59.950
The Militia's people are still drinking...

00:09:59.950 --> 00:10:04.240
They're getting drunk even quicker while they're space sick.

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:07.620
Things would be so much easier if Mr. Horace were here...

00:10:07.620 --> 00:10:08.830
Where are you going with that?

00:10:08.830 --> 00:10:10.630
We're just throwin' it outside!

00:10:10.630 --> 00:10:13.340
It'll be a good capsule for people, don't you think?

00:10:13.750 --> 00:10:14.920
What are you doing in there?

00:10:14.920 --> 00:10:18.130
The Inglessa men say they want to float home in a sake barrel.

00:10:18.130 --> 00:10:19.550
That's absurd!

00:10:19.550 --> 00:10:23.140
- Is there a problem?
- Have you always been this stupid?

00:10:23.140 --> 00:10:27.640
- The people capsule's all done!
- Best of luck to you!

00:10:33.520 --> 00:10:35.730
This is the best idea ever!

00:10:37.240 --> 00:10:39.240
Ahh, crikey... it's cold...

00:10:39.740 --> 00:10:42.120
How do I close the glass cover?

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:44.240
My eyes hurt!

00:10:44.240 --> 00:10:45.620
Hey, somebody help me!

00:10:50.620 --> 00:10:52.420
The target is way too small!

00:11:02.930 --> 00:11:04.140
Injecting the Oxygen...

00:11:04.550 --> 00:11:05.850
Life readings...

00:11:06.220 --> 00:11:07.350
Good...

00:11:08.430 --> 00:11:09.730
...Thank Goodness.

00:11:10.230 --> 00:11:13.230
Honestly now, these Terrans are too much to handle...

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:19.320
One could say that the Militia's men are rather brave, at least...

00:11:19.320 --> 00:11:21.240
But their goals may be a bit questionable.

00:11:21.240 --> 00:11:25.830
Not really. What the Moonrace calls stupidity is the same as what they call blind courage!

00:11:25.830 --> 00:11:30.250
I suppose such fearless ambition is what will allow us to advance.

00:11:30.750 --> 00:11:33.040
That's simply the way adults are, isn't it?

00:11:34.630 --> 00:11:37.920
Anybody on the bridge must take a seat! Including you, Lady Lily!

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:39.720
My! How Scary...

00:11:39.720 --> 00:11:44.930
We can't do work that's worthy of our pay if you amateurs keep getting in our way!

00:11:44.930 --> 00:11:46.720
Yeah, yeah.

00:11:47.350 --> 00:11:50.140
My face is frozen... please, be gentle...

00:11:50.140 --> 00:11:54.150
Your face appears to have been burned. It could be frostbite, you know.

00:11:54.440 --> 00:11:56.520
You've gotten really good at this, Sis.

00:11:56.520 --> 00:12:00.440
After all of your work in the field hospital, you must've had a lot of practice.

00:12:00.440 --> 00:12:01.950
The hospital?

00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:04.610
I heard it was actually Lady Lily who volunteered you to do that work.

00:12:04.610 --> 00:12:07.620
I never imagined that Queen Dianna had to endure that...

00:12:07.620 --> 00:12:11.330
Hold on, was that person actually Dianna?

00:12:11.330 --> 00:12:14.620
It's the sort of thing Lady Lily Borjarno would do, coming from the background that she does...

00:12:15.250 --> 00:12:16.330
How is he doing?

00:12:16.330 --> 00:12:17.750
He's already doing better.

00:12:17.750 --> 00:12:19.920
I'm going to go and service the Mechanical Dolls.

00:12:19.920 --> 00:12:20.920
Go on ahead, then.

00:12:21.340 --> 00:12:24.220
- Lady Kihel...
- Yes?

00:12:24.220 --> 00:12:27.050
The Lieutenant would like to have a word with you.

00:12:27.050 --> 00:12:28.050
Oh?

00:12:40.150 --> 00:12:43.280
Colonel Michael, Open this door and we can negotiate!

00:12:43.280 --> 00:12:45.160
Colonel Michael, please open up!

00:12:45.160 --> 00:12:50.580
The problem, Colonel, is that there's more to a journey between the Earth and the Moon than switching a few thrusters.

00:12:50.580 --> 00:12:53.370
You must also factor in the gravitational pull of all of the other celestial bodies!

00:12:53.370 --> 00:12:55.170
Don't bother lecturing me.

00:12:55.170 --> 00:12:57.040
Return the Willgem to the Earth.

00:12:57.040 --> 00:12:58.170
Forgive us.

00:12:58.170 --> 00:12:59.880
How could you use Kihel as a hostage?

00:12:59.880 --> 00:13:01.670
And who are you trying to deceive?

00:13:01.670 --> 00:13:04.840
All of us understand that the girl here is in fact Dianna Soriel.

00:13:04.840 --> 00:13:07.260
Sir Guin, there would be no reason...

00:13:07.260 --> 00:13:12.060
For someone such as yourself to transport a temporary secretary all the way to the moon!

00:13:12.060 --> 00:13:13.980
Is my sister going to be alright?

00:13:13.980 --> 00:13:16.480
The Colonel isn't a reckless person. She'll be fine.

00:13:16.480 --> 00:13:21.780
I guess I've underestimated the effects of space. When we left our homeground behind...

00:13:21.780 --> 00:13:25.070
...even our normally steady tempered Colonel began to panic.

00:13:25.070 --> 00:13:27.160
Does that mean we're going back?

00:13:27.160 --> 00:13:28.740
Don't be foolish!

00:13:28.740 --> 00:13:34.450
As long as the moon remains such distant threat, it would be impossible to stop the battle with Dianna Counter.

00:13:34.450 --> 00:13:38.250
That is why we must continue on this course.

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:40.250
Impressive, Sir Guin.

00:13:40.250 --> 00:13:43.760
You're truly our brave and heroic leader.

00:13:43.760 --> 00:13:45.760
Colonel Michael! Colonel Michael!

00:13:45.760 --> 00:13:47.050
What is it?

00:13:47.050 --> 00:13:48.840
Wouldn't you agree that I would personally...

00:13:48.840 --> 00:13:52.760
Make a much better hostage for your objective than Lady Kihel would?

00:13:52.760 --> 00:13:55.770
Hey, why can't we use White Doll to break inside there?

00:13:55.770 --> 00:13:57.060
That won't work.

00:13:57.060 --> 00:13:58.480
Outside the ship's a total vacuum...

00:13:58.480 --> 00:14:00.480
With a temperature difference of over 400 degrees.

00:14:00.480 --> 00:14:01.570
Is this some sort of coup d'etat?

00:14:01.570 --> 00:14:03.360
Well, that's not quite it.

00:14:03.360 --> 00:14:07.070
If you are unable to battle them face to face, then a better answer may be to cleanse their air.

00:14:07.070 --> 00:14:09.450
Cleanse their air?

00:14:09.450 --> 00:14:12.660
However, don't you agree that Sir Guin is correct?

00:14:12.660 --> 00:14:14.870
It's imperative that we reach the moon in order to negotiate with them.

00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:20.040
Flying directly into enemy territory with just one ship is far too rash.

00:14:20.040 --> 00:14:24.750
Then, if you believe me to be Queen Dianna, the moon is also my homeland.

00:14:24.750 --> 00:14:28.050
Put your worries aside and trust me.

00:14:28.680 --> 00:14:33.350
And otherwise, if I am actually Kihel Heim, then I'm useless to use as a hostage anyhow.

00:14:33.350 --> 00:14:36.770
Either way, what you're attempting to do now is all in vain.

00:14:38.270 --> 00:14:39.480
What is this?

00:14:39.480 --> 00:14:41.350
Hey, Bruno and Jacop!

00:14:41.350 --> 00:14:42.770
The air's being drained out!

00:14:42.770 --> 00:14:43.860
How?

00:14:43.860 --> 00:14:45.360
Bruno, do you know the cause?

00:14:45.360 --> 00:14:48.570
It's being controlled from outside!

00:14:48.570 --> 00:14:52.870
Guin Rhineford, Don't you realize Dianna Soriel is in here!?

00:14:52.870 --> 00:14:56.870
Colonel, we already told you she's Miss Kihel Heim.

00:14:57.080 --> 00:14:58.580
Will he fall for it?

00:14:58.580 --> 00:15:02.540
Even if he does, he may shoot her if he gets upset.

00:15:02.750 --> 00:15:05.460
And will you be ready to take responsibility for that, Sir Guin?

00:15:05.460 --> 00:15:07.840
He can't afford to do a thing like that.

00:15:07.840 --> 00:15:08.970
That's exactly right.

00:15:08.970 --> 00:15:11.760
Shh... I'm hearing movement inside there...

00:15:11.760 --> 00:15:15.060
Do they have an animal on the bridge or something?

00:15:15.850 --> 00:15:17.350
Will that be alright?

00:15:17.350 --> 00:15:19.350
They only brought the girl with them...

00:15:37.240 --> 00:15:38.750
Are you unharmed?

00:15:38.750 --> 00:15:40.580
Is that Lieutenant Harry's doing?

00:15:40.580 --> 00:15:42.040
Thank goodness!

00:15:42.040 --> 00:15:46.670
Please, tell them that such acts of resistance won't help anything.

00:15:46.670 --> 00:15:48.460
Jacop, Bruno...

00:15:48.460 --> 00:15:49.840
Is our flight still on course?

00:15:49.840 --> 00:15:52.260
I don't think they harmed anything.

00:15:52.260 --> 00:15:53.760
Our flight-path hasn't been altered.

00:15:53.760 --> 00:15:55.550
Take the mechanical dolls!

00:15:55.550 --> 00:15:57.560
Forget about Mustache and the Gold Type...

00:15:57.560 --> 00:16:02.060
...but take the Kapool and Borjarnon! We can use those.

00:16:02.060 --> 00:16:03.980
A Kapool can hold seven or eight of us!

00:16:03.980 --> 00:16:05.860
These guys want to take our Borjarnon!?

00:16:05.860 --> 00:16:07.150
Don't worry about them.

00:16:07.150 --> 00:16:08.150
How could you say that?

00:16:08.150 --> 00:16:10.070
They don't know even know how to control them!

00:16:10.070 --> 00:16:13.450
We'll view this as a test of their space capabilities.

00:16:13.450 --> 00:16:14.950
Lieutenant, what are you doing?

00:16:15.570 --> 00:16:19.160
Alright, that takes care of that. Four or five people can join me in this one!

00:16:19.160 --> 00:16:21.160
There's room for one more here!

00:16:21.160 --> 00:16:26.040
Colonel, we're much too far from the earth for you to possibly reach there on your own!

00:16:26.040 --> 00:16:27.670
You won't be able to make it!

00:16:27.670 --> 00:16:32.050
It's no more risky than your plans of driving a lone spacecraft directly into enemy territory!

00:16:32.050 --> 00:16:37.550
And Earth is still in plain sight from here, just as Mount Ark's in plain sight from Vicinity!

00:16:37.550 --> 00:16:39.470
I know that...

00:16:39.470 --> 00:16:41.980
But please realize that's because of how massive earth itself is!

00:16:41.980 --> 00:16:45.270
If Ameria's about the size of my palm now, then...

00:16:45.270 --> 00:16:47.860
We're not like you! We're Earth's native people!

00:16:47.860 --> 00:16:51.360
Earthlings were meant to live on Earth! That's what makes us Earthlings!

00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:53.950
We've had enough of space!

00:16:53.950 --> 00:16:56.240
We have no intention of being dragged to the moon!

00:16:56.240 --> 00:16:58.450
Colonel, you must reconsider!

00:16:58.450 --> 00:17:02.370
If you don't open the shutter on your own, we'll be forced to blow it open for you!

00:17:02.370 --> 00:17:05.870
If you wreck that thing, I'll hunt you like a dog!

00:17:05.870 --> 00:17:07.670
Close shutter number three!

00:17:08.380 --> 00:17:09.670
What can we do, Loran?

00:17:09.670 --> 00:17:12.460
They are overloaded by a factor of five!

00:17:12.460 --> 00:17:15.840
And when you consider how aggressive those men were acting...

00:17:15.840 --> 00:17:18.470
They'll run through their oxygen even faster.

00:17:18.470 --> 00:17:20.060
- Is that true?
- It is.

00:17:20.060 --> 00:17:22.060
That's not the main problem...

00:17:36.780 --> 00:17:37.740
There!

00:17:37.740 --> 00:17:40.160
It's so close that I could reach out and touch it!

00:17:40.160 --> 00:17:43.660
The real earth looks beautiful without all those names and numbers written on it!

00:17:43.660 --> 00:17:45.750
Yeah, that's right.

00:17:45.750 --> 00:17:48.170
- You'll be launching?
- Yes.

00:17:48.170 --> 00:17:49.670
What should be done now?

00:17:49.670 --> 00:17:53.050
Well, we already cleansed their air, so I guess we just wait now.

00:17:53.050 --> 00:17:54.170
This isn't a joke!

00:17:54.170 --> 00:17:55.760
And what about our Borjarnons!?

00:17:55.760 --> 00:17:58.340
We cleansed their air, so we'll let them go.

00:17:58.340 --> 00:18:00.680
Based on the way you were acting...

00:18:00.680 --> 00:18:04.270
I thought you were going to help us reclaim the Borjarnons!

00:18:04.270 --> 00:18:08.060
Right now, the most important thing is that we make it clear that acts of mutiny are a useless gesture.

00:18:08.060 --> 00:18:10.150
Then what about Michael and the rest?

00:18:10.150 --> 00:18:12.940
Traditionally they would have been executed. This spares us that task.

00:18:12.940 --> 00:18:13.940
Executed?

00:18:13.940 --> 00:18:15.940
Is mutiny not a capital offense?

00:18:15.940 --> 00:18:19.450
That's terrible. You're oversimplifying the matter too much.

00:18:19.450 --> 00:18:21.570
I'm also against it.

00:18:21.950 --> 00:18:23.450
What are you planning?

00:18:23.450 --> 00:18:24.370
Loran!

00:18:24.370 --> 00:18:26.750
Just be sure to bring back the Borjarnons!

00:18:26.750 --> 00:18:28.160
That's my intent!

00:18:32.040 --> 00:18:34.170
As I thought, it's completely different from the sake barrel.

00:18:34.170 --> 00:18:36.670
With this, we'll have no trouble getting back to earth!

00:18:36.670 --> 00:18:38.680
We also have food in the container.

00:18:38.680 --> 00:18:40.550
Are we being followed?

00:18:40.550 --> 00:18:42.760
Is it the Mustache?

00:18:42.760 --> 00:18:46.770
All of you, give me space! Don't get in the way of the pilot!

00:18:51.560 --> 00:18:53.360
Colonel, please return now!

00:18:53.360 --> 00:18:55.150
If you don't, you'll be executed!

00:18:55.150 --> 00:18:57.070
What's that? Execution?

00:18:57.780 --> 00:19:00.660
Please, wait! We can still talk about it!

00:19:00.660 --> 00:19:02.240
That was our warning shot.

00:19:02.240 --> 00:19:05.240
If you don't go back now, the next volley will hit the target!

00:19:05.240 --> 00:19:08.250
I will not turn back alone. I intend to take you all back with me.

00:19:08.250 --> 00:19:10.750
Really? That's quite a shame.

00:19:10.750 --> 00:19:13.170
Your negotiations have failed, Moonrace!

00:19:19.670 --> 00:19:21.050
Is this the way to use those mobile suits?

00:19:23.470 --> 00:19:25.350
- You did it!
- Just as we'd expect from the lieutenant!

00:19:25.850 --> 00:19:26.850
Amazing!

00:19:30.560 --> 00:19:33.150
If I had been expecting this, I would've brought my shield!

00:19:38.570 --> 00:19:42.860
The Militia's pride seems to be giving them an edge over the White Doll here in space.

00:19:42.860 --> 00:19:44.450
Laura is a gentle person.

00:19:44.450 --> 00:19:48.450
Because they're his comrades, he's confused and unsure of what he should do.

00:19:48.660 --> 00:19:51.080
However, things can't continue like this.

00:19:52.960 --> 00:19:56.460
Loran, you absolutely MUST be careful as long as you still have that bomb with you!

00:19:56.460 --> 00:19:59.840
You should have the advantage in a space fight... because you're part of the Moonrace.

00:20:05.260 --> 00:20:06.680
Is that all?

00:20:09.350 --> 00:20:14.350
If you cause the nuclear bombs to detonate, Colonel, then the Willgem and everyone else will be killed!

00:20:25.570 --> 00:20:27.240
This will do it!

00:20:33.870 --> 00:20:34.960
DON'T DO IT!

00:20:54.270 --> 00:20:56.560
That was a bit risky, Loran.

00:20:56.560 --> 00:20:57.650
Harry!

00:20:57.650 --> 00:20:58.860
What did you do?

00:20:58.860 --> 00:21:00.280
Oh, nothing.

00:21:00.280 --> 00:21:06.450
I suspect they're suffering from oxygen deprivation since there's so many of them crammed in those cockpits.

00:21:06.860 --> 00:21:09.080
My head... it hurts...

00:21:09.450 --> 00:21:12.080
She wants to take a photo to commemorate the occasion.

00:21:12.080 --> 00:21:14.540
That sounds like a good idea, doesn't it?

00:21:15.370 --> 00:21:16.870
Sir Guin?

00:21:16.870 --> 00:21:19.170
Well, I'm not going to enforce capital punishment on them.

00:21:19.670 --> 00:21:22.380
Well, which one do you think she is?

00:21:22.380 --> 00:21:24.050
The one who just left this room?

00:21:24.050 --> 00:21:28.340
Yes. Is it Miss Kihel, or Queen Dianna?

00:21:28.340 --> 00:21:31.060
I don't really know for sure.

00:21:31.060 --> 00:21:35.060
Alright! Now everyone, please look at the camera!

00:21:35.560 --> 00:21:37.850
Okay, Let's do it. Peace!

00:21:37.850 --> 00:21:39.650
PEACE!

00:21:41.360 --> 00:21:43.360
Ahh, there we go.

00:21:43.360 --> 00:21:45.070
Colonel, is anything wrong?

00:21:45.070 --> 00:21:47.360
No...

00:21:49.070 --> 00:21:52.080
Ahh, that's a photo of your family.

00:21:59.460 --> 00:22:00.670
I will...

00:22:01.250 --> 00:22:05.550
I will... Nina... Matthew...

00:22:05.550 --> 00:22:08.760
Your father will most definitely return home to you.

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:34.540
<b><i>Binetsu ga samenai mama</i></b>

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:34.540
<b>As if unawoken from a slight fever</b>

00:22:34.540 --> 00:22:40.790
<b><i>Utsumuku shounen no hitomi wa</i></b>

00:22:34.540 --> 00:22:40.790
<b>The eyes of the boy hanging his head</b>

00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:46.510
<b><i>Kokoro no umi mitsumete</i></b>

00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:46.510
<b>Gaze upon the sea of his heart</b>

00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:50.510
<b><i>Shizuka ni hohoenderu</i></b>

00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:50.510
<b>And smile silently</b>

00:22:52.220 --> 00:22:57.020
<b><i>Umare kuru mono kiete yuku mono</i></b>

00:22:52.220 --> 00:22:57.020
<b>What is born, and what fades away</b>

00:22:57.020 --> 00:23:03.230
<b><i>Subete wa sadame no furiko no haba</i></b>

00:22:57.020 --> 00:23:03.230
<b>Are but the sway of the pendulum of fate</b>

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:08.950
<b><i>Zasetsu no yami o tsukinuke mietekuru</i></b>

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:08.950
<b>Piercing the darkness of frustration, he begins to see it</b>

00:23:08.950 --> 00:23:14.530
<b><i>Sore ga hikari no shinjitsu</i></b>

00:23:08.950 --> 00:23:14.530
<b>It is the reality of the light</b>

00:23:14.530 --> 00:23:16.870
<b><i>Aura</i></b>

00:23:14.530 --> 00:23:16.870
<b>Aura</b>

00:23:16.870 --> 00:23:25.340
<b><i>Yoake totomoni wasuresareru hoshi ni sasagu</i></b>

00:23:16.870 --> 00:23:25.340
<b>Together with dawn, he gives an offering to the stars that will be forgotten</b>

00:23:25.340 --> 00:23:27.630
<b><i>Aura</i></b>

00:23:25.340 --> 00:23:27.630
<b>Aura</b>

00:23:27.630 --> 00:23:35.510
<b><i>Shijou no ai wa chiisana sono te no naka ni aru</i></b>

00:23:27.630 --> 00:23:35.510
<b>History's love lies in his tiny hands</b>

00:23:40.100 --> 00:23:45.940
<i>We receive word that Queen Dianna has escaped to the artificial satellite, Mistletoe.</i>

00:23:46.860 --> 00:23:49.780
<i>And so myself and Lady Sochie set off to rescue her.</i>

00:23:49.780 --> 00:23:54.490
<i>However, the squad led by the Samurai of the Moon, Gym Ghingnham, also arrives...</i>

00:23:55.070 --> 00:23:56.870
<i>...with the Mahiroo Mobile Suits.</i>

00:23:59.000 --> 00:24:02.750
<i>Next time... on </i>TURN A GUNDAM...<i>
"Gateway To The Moon"</i>

00:24:03.580 --> 00:24:05.960
"The wind trembles."

00:24:03.790 --> 00:24:08.420
<b>Gateway To The Moon</b>
